# Deployments & Environments (Render, Vercel, Supabase)

Use this guide when configuring, modifying, or managing deployments across branches and environments.

## 1. Environments & Branch Architecture

| Environment | Branch | Backend (Render) | Frontend (Vercel) | Database (Supabase) |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| **Production** | `main` | `board-game-hub-api` (`https://board-game-hub-api.onrender.com`) | `https://board-game-hub.vercel.app` | Supabase Prod |
| **Development** | `dev` | `board-game-hub-api-dev` (`https://board-game-hub-api-dev.onrender.com`) | `https://board-game-hub-dev.vercel.app` | Supabase Dev |
| **Preview** | `pull_request` | Render Preview Environments (`render.yaml`) | Vercel PR Previews | Dev DB / Isolated |

---

## 2. Render Blueprint Specification (`render.yaml`)

Both backend services must be defined in `render.yaml` as synchronized twin services:

```yaml
services:
  - type: web
    name: board-game-hub-api
    branch: main
    env: docker
    dockerfilePath: ./backend/Dockerfile
    dockerContext: .
    region: oregon 
    plan: free
    envVars:
      - key: ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT
        value: Production
      - key: ASPNETCORE_URLS
        value: http://+:8080
      - key: ConnectionStrings__DefaultConnection
        sync: false # Set in Render Dashboard
      - key: Jwt__Key
        sync: false

  - type: web
    name: board-game-hub-api-dev
    branch: dev
    env: docker
    dockerfilePath: ./backend/Dockerfile
    dockerContext: .
    region: oregon 
    plan: free
    envVars:
      - key: ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT
        value: Development
      - key: ASPNETCORE_URLS
        value: http://+:8080
      - key: ConnectionStrings__DefaultConnection
        sync: false # Set in Render Dashboard (Supabase Dev)
      - key: Jwt__Key
        sync: false
```

---

## 3. CI/CD Pipeline & Migration Sequence

For any deployment triggering via GitHub Actions (`.github/workflows/deploy-backend-render.yml`):

1. **Test & Build**: Run all .NET backend tests with `--no-build -c Release`.
2. **EF Migration Bundle**: Automatically generate `efbundle` and apply migrations to the target Supabase environment (`production` on `main`, `development` on `dev`) **prior** to triggering the Render deploy hook.
3. **Trigger Deploy**: Invoke the respective `RENDER_DEPLOY_HOOK_URL_PROD` or `RENDER_DEPLOY_HOOK_URL_DEV`.

---

## 4. Operational Commands (GitHub CLI)

- **List active deployment workflow runs:**
  ```powershell
  gh run list --workflow "Deploy Backend to Render" --branch dev
  ```
- **Watch run execution:**
  ```powershell
  gh run watch <run_id>
  ```
- **Trigger manual deployment:**
  ```powershell
  gh workflow run "deploy-backend-render.yml" --ref dev
  ```
